AS2R: Another Sonic 2 Remake for AmigaOS 3 - @RELEASE_VERSION@
===========================================================

The Amiga OpenSurge engine, ready to play AS2R: Another Sonic 2 Remake,
a fan game made with the Open Surge Engine. No separate engine install is
needed.

THIS ARCHIVE HAS NONE OF THE GAME'S OWN FILES. Its makers have not said
they may be passed on, so they are not. Download the game yourself, from
its page:


  https://sonicfangameshq.com/forums/showcase/as2r-another-sonic-2-remake-sage-22-demo.1389/

  file     Another Sonic 2 Remake Android Compatible.zip
  size     121434129 bytes
  sha256   dd79b04d12164ff5572a0abed1f38930e3d102d498d9113f82aed00a3a9eece2

The game, its characters and its music belong to their makers and owners;
it is not made by or for SEGA.

Installing
----------
Double-click Install-AS2R beside the AS2R drawer. It checks the CPU,
FPU and GFOpenGPU, asks where the AS2R drawer should go (Work:Games is
offered), copies the engine there, and then asks for the game you
downloaded:

- the archive itself: the Installer checks its size and unpacks it with
  SYS:Utilities/GFOpenCompress (part of AmiCradle) into the drawer;
- or the folder "Another Sonic 2 Remake" that unpacking it made;
- or a game.zip made from the download on another computer with the port's
  scripts/prepare-amiga-port.sh.

It checks the folder's name and the sizes of a few of its files, then
copies the game's files into AS2R/Game, leaving out the Windows program
files. It then updates the menu script for OpenSurge 0.6.1 with
Tools/PatchMenu.rexx (ARexx; RexxMast is started if it is not running) and
adds Tools/surge.cfg. Running Install-AS2R again replaces or keeps those
files.

The Installer can check the download's SHA-256 on the Amiga with
Tools/SHA256, which comes in this archive: given the archive, it asks
(Check it is the default) before unpacking it; given the unpacked
folder, it asks whether you still have the archive and checks that.
It takes a few minutes on a 68040. Without the archive, the folder is
checked by the sizes of a few of its files only.

The same check from a Shell, in the AS2R drawer:
  Tools/SHA256 "Another Sonic 2 Remake Android Compatible.zip" EXPECT=<SHA-256 above>
or on another computer:
  sha256sum "Another Sonic 2 Remake Android Compatible.zip"

What is in the drawer
---------------------
StartGame   starts the game (once its files are installed)
Engine/     the OpenSurge engine (below)
Game/       the game's own files, from your download (Install-AS2R)
Tools/      what Install-AS2R uses (SHA256 checks the download)
Licences/   licences and the engine's source

What it needs
-------------
- AmigaOS 3.2 (Installer 43.3 or newer for Install-AS2R)
- a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU
- GFOpenGPU: LIBS:GFOpenGPU/GL.module and SDL2.module (as on AmiCradle)
- about 480 MB free on the hard disk, and plenty of Fast RAM

The engine
----------
Engine/ is Amiga OpenSurge, Open Surge Engine 0.6.1.3 for AmigaOS 3,
exactly as released:

  release   @ENGINE_REPO@ @ENGINE_TAG@
  commit    @ENGINE_COMMIT@
  archive   @ENGINE_ASSET@
  sha256    @ENGINE_SHA256@
  program   Engine/opensurge
  sha256    @ENGINE_BINARY_SHA256@
  compiler  @ENGINE_COMPILER@

No separate engine install is needed: StartGame runs this copy. The engine
keeps its settings (surge.prefs), logfile.txt and the game's compatibility
pack in the Game drawer when the game was installed from your download, or
in Engine/.userdata with a game.zip. Licences/SOURCE.txt says where its
source is.

Starting and playing
--------------------
Double-click StartGame in the AS2R drawer. From a Shell, CD to the
drawer first, then Execute StartGame. F10 switches between a window and
the full screen. Leave the game from its own menu (Esc brings it up in
most games).

